1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,808
SARAH:

2
00:00:00,808 --> 00:00:01,192
Hello.

3
00:00:01,192 --> 00:00:03,090
Children's Engineering Workshops.

4
00:00:03,090 --> 00:00:03,140
FATHER:

5
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:04,333
Oh hello.

6
00:00:04,333 --> 00:00:08,890
I wanted some information about the workshops in the school holidays.

7
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:09,305
SARAH:

8
00:00:09,305 --> 00:00:09,720
Sure.

9
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:10,089
FATHER:

10
00:00:10,089 --> 00:00:12,670
I have two daughters who are interested.

11
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:17,680
The younger one's Lydia, she's four – do you take children as young as that?

12
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:18,255
SARAH:

13
00:00:18,255 --> 00:00:24,000
Yes, our Tiny Engineers workshop is for four to five-year-olds.

14
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:24,284
FATHER:

15
00:00:24,284 --> 00:00:26,270
What sorts of activities do they do?

16
00:00:26,270 --> 00:00:26,633
SARAH:

17
00:00:26,633 --> 00:00:27,358
All sorts.

18
00:00:27,358 --> 00:00:32,435
For example, they work together to design a special cover that goes?round an

19
00:00:32,435 --> 00:00:32,798
egg,

20
00:00:32,798 --> 00:00:37,149
so that when it's inside they can drop it from a height

21
00:00:37,149 --> 00:00:38,600
and it doesn't break.

22
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:42,630
Well, sometimes it does break but that's part of the fun!

23
00:00:42,630 --> 00:00:43,171
FATHER:

24
00:00:43,171 --> 00:00:43,713
Right.

25
00:00:43,713 --> 00:00:46,420
And Lydia loves building things.

26
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:50,150
Is there any opportunity for her to do that?

27
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:50,486
SARAH:

28
00:00:50,486 --> 00:00:54,860
Well, they have a competition to see who can make the highest tower.

29
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:58,000
You'd be amazed how high they can go.

30
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:58,235
FATHER:

31
00:00:58,235 --> 00:00:58,470
Right.

32
00:00:58,470 --> 00:00:58,809
SARAH:

33
00:00:58,809 --> 00:01:02,540
But they're learning all the time as well as having fun.

34
00:01:02,540 --> 00:01:07,364
For example, one thing they do is to design and build a car that's

35
00:01:07,364 --> 00:01:08,742
attached to a balloon,

36
00:01:08,742 --> 00:01:12,877
and the force of the air in that actually powers the car

37
00:01:12,877 --> 00:01:14,600
and makes it move along.

38
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:17,310
They go really fast too.

39
00:01:17,310 --> 00:01:17,804
FATHER:

40
00:01:17,804 --> 00:01:20,770
OK, well, all this sounds perfect.

41
00:01:20,770 --> 00:01:21,294
FATHER:

42
00:01:21,294 --> 00:01:22,343
Now Carly,

43
00:01:22,343 --> 00:01:27,586
that's my older daughter, has just had her seventh birthday,

44
00:01:27,586 --> 00:01:31,780
so presumably she'd be in a different group?

45
00:01:31,780 --> 00:01:32,235
SARAH:

46
00:01:32,235 --> 00:01:35,420
Yes, she'd be in the Junior Engineers.

47
00:01:35,420 --> 00:01:38,480
That's for children from six to eight.

48
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:38,780
FATHER:

49
00:01:38,780 --> 00:01:41,480
And do they do the same sorts of activities?

50
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:41,860
SARAH:

51
00:01:41,860 --> 00:01:43,380
Some are the same,

52
00:01:43,380 --> 00:01:45,280
but a bit more advanced.

53
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:51,068
So they work out how to build model vehicles, things like cars and trucks,

54
00:01:51,068 --> 00:01:56,856
but also how to construct animals using the same sorts of material and technique,

55
00:01:56,856 --> 00:02:02,230
and then they learn how they can program them and make them move.

56
00:02:02,230 --> 00:02:02,505
FATHER:

57
00:02:02,505 --> 00:02:04,430
So they learn a bit of coding?

58
00:02:04,430 --> 00:02:04,797
SARAH:

59
00:02:04,797 --> 00:02:05,530
They do.

60
00:02:05,530 --> 00:02:07,730
They pick it up really quickly.

61
00:02:07,730 --> 00:02:10,215
We're there to help if they need it,

62
00:02:10,215 --> 00:02:12,390
but they learn from one another too.

63
00:02:12,390 --> 00:02:12,861
FATHER:

64
00:02:12,861 --> 00:02:13,332
Right.

65
00:02:13,332 --> 00:02:16,160
And do they have competitions too?

66
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:16,587
SARAH:

67
00:02:16,587 --> 00:02:21,710
Yes, with the Junior Engineers, it's to use recycled materials like card

68
00:02:21,710 --> 00:02:24,272
and wood to build a bridge,

69
00:02:24,272 --> 00:02:27,260
and the longest one gets a prize.

70
00:02:27,260 --> 00:02:27,594
FATHER:

71
00:02:27,594 --> 00:02:28,596
That sounds fun.

72
00:02:28,596 --> 00:02:30,600
I wouldn't mind doing that myself!

73
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:31,020
SARAH:

74
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:33,957
Then they have something a bit different,

75
00:02:33,957 --> 00:02:38,573
which is to think up an idea for a five-minute movie

76
00:02:38,573 --> 00:02:41,930
and then film it, using special animation software.

77
00:02:41,930 --> 00:02:44,410
You'd be amazed what they come up with.

78
00:02:44,410 --> 00:02:44,690
FATHER:

79
00:02:44,690 --> 00:02:45,528
And of course,

80
00:02:45,528 --> 00:02:49,441
that's something they can put on their phone and take home to show all

81
00:02:49,441 --> 00:02:50,000
their friends.

82
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:50,350
SARAH:

83
00:02:50,350 --> 00:02:50,700
Exactly.

84
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:55,250
And then they also build a robot in the shape of a human,

85
00:02:55,250 --> 00:03:00,150
and they decorate it and program it so that it can move its arms

86
00:03:00,150 --> 00:03:00,850
and legs.

87
00:03:00,850 --> 00:03:01,262
FATHER:

88
00:03:01,262 --> 00:03:01,673
Perfect.

89
00:03:01,673 --> 00:03:05,790
So, is it the same price as the Tiny Engineers?

90
00:03:05,790 --> 00:03:06,165
SARAH:

91
00:03:06,165 --> 00:03:08,037
It's just a bit more:

92
00:03:08,037 --> 00:03:09,910
￡50 for the five weeks.

93
00:03:09,910 --> 00:03:10,162
FATHER:

94
00:03:10,162 --> 00:03:12,180
And are the classes on a Monday too?

95
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:12,541
SARAH:

96
00:03:12,541 --> 00:03:13,987
They used to be,

97
00:03:13,987 --> 00:03:19,047
but we found it didn't give our staff enough time to clear up after

98
00:03:19,047 --> 00:03:20,131
the first workshop,

99
00:03:20,131 --> 00:03:22,300
so we moved them to Wednesdays.

100
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:26,060
The classes are held in the morning from ten to eleven.

101
00:03:26,060 --> 00:03:26,479
FATHER:

102
00:03:26,479 --> 00:03:26,897
OK.

103
00:03:26,897 --> 00:03:28,990
That's better for me actually.

104
00:03:28,990 --> 00:03:31,170
And what about the location?

105
00:03:31,170 --> 00:03:34,000
Where exactly are the workshops held?

106
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:34,375
SARAH:

107
00:03:34,375 --> 00:03:39,244
They're in building 10A – there's a big sign on the door, you can't

108
00:03:39,244 --> 00:03:39,993
miss it,

109
00:03:39,993 --> 00:03:42,240
and that's in Fradstone Industrial Estate.

110
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:42,670
FATHER:

111
00:03:42,670 --> 00:03:43,100
Sorry?

112
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:45,718
SARAH:

113
00:03:45,718 --> 00:03:53,570
Fradstone – that's F-R-A-D-S-T-O-N-E.

114
00:03:53,570 --> 00:03:54,019
FATHER:

115
00:03:54,019 --> 00:03:56,710
And that's in Grasford, isn't it?

116
00:03:56,710 --> 00:03:57,073
SARAH:

117
00:03:57,073 --> 00:03:58,890
Yes, up past the station.

118
00:03:58,890 --> 00:03:59,191
FATHER:

119
00:03:59,191 --> 00:04:01,600
And will I have any parking problems there?

120
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:02,050
SARAH:

121
00:04:02,050 --> 00:04:04,300
No, there's always plenty available.

122
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:08,000
So would you like to enrol Lydia and Carly now?

123
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:08,435
FATHER:

124
00:04:08,435 --> 00:04:08,870
OK.

125
00:04:08,870 --> 00:04:09,136
SARAH:

126
00:04:09,136 --> 00:04:11,000
So can I have your full name …
